"""Printed 139: motion example continuation and full Exercise 5.2."""
from math12_reviewed_unit1 import heading,paragraph,page
from math12_reviewed_higher_derivatives import eq,note
QUESTIONS=[
 r'Find the vector derivative: (a) \(F⃗(t)=tî+t^2ĵ+(t+t^3)k̂\); (b) \(F⃗(s)=(sî+s^2ĵ+s^2k̂)+(2s^2î-sĵ+3k̂)\); (c) \(F⃗(\theta)=\cos\theta[î+\tan\thetaĵ+3k̂]\).',
 r'Find second derivatives: (a) \(t^2î+3t^3ĵ-8t^2k̂\); (b) \((3+s^2)î-(s+1)^2ĵ+3s^4k̂\); (c) \(\ln xî-x^2k̂\); (d) \(\sin^2\thetaî-\cos^2\thetaĵ\).',
 r'Differentiate the scalar functions: (a) \(f(x)=[xî+(x+1)ĵ]\cdot[2xî-3x^2ĵ]\); (b) \(g(x)=|\sin xî-2xĵ+\cos xk̂|\).',
 r'Find velocity, acceleration, speed and direction of motion at the indicated t: (a) \(r⃗(t)=tî+t^2ĵ+2tk̂\), t = 1; (b) \(r⃗(t)=\cos tî+\sin tĵ+3tk̂\), t = π/4; (c) \(r⃗(t)=e^tî+e^{-t}ĵ+e^{2t}k̂\), t = ln 2.',
 r'If F(t) is a differentiable vector function and F(t) ≠ 0, show \(\frac d{dt}\frac{F⃗(t)}{|F⃗(t)|}=\frac{F⃗′(t)}{|F⃗(t)|}-\frac{[F⃗(t)\cdot F⃗′(t)]F⃗(t)}{|F⃗(t)|^3}\).'
]
STEPS=[
 ['Differentiate each component with respect to its stated parameter.', '(a) The derivatives of t,t²,t+t³ are 1,2t,1+3t². Therefore F⃗′ = î+2tĵ+(1+3t²)k̂.', '(b) Combine the input vectors first: F⃗(s) = (s+2s²)î+(s²−s)ĵ+(s²+3)k̂.', 'Differentiate: F⃗′(s) = (1+4s)î+(2s−1)ĵ+2sk̂.', '(c) On the original domain cos θ ≠ 0, expand to F⃗(θ) = cos θî+sin θĵ+3cos θk̂.', 'Thus F⃗′(θ) = −sin θî+cos θĵ−3sin θk̂.', 'The simplified formula extends across excluded points, but the printed tan θ expression and its derivative are defined only for cos θ ≠ 0.'],
 ['Take first derivatives, then differentiate again.', '(a) F⃗′ = 2tî+9t²ĵ−16tk̂; F⃗″ = 2î+18tĵ−16k̂.', '(b) F⃗′ = 2sî−2(s+1)ĵ+12s³k̂; F⃗″ = 2î−2ĵ+36s²k̂.', '(c) ln x requires x > 0. F⃗′ = x⁻¹î−2xk̂; F⃗″ = −x⁻²î−2k̂, on x > 0.', '(d) The derivative of sin²θ is 2sin θcos θ, and of −cos²θ is also 2sin θcos θ.', 'Thus F⃗′(θ) = sin(2θ)(î+ĵ).', 'Differentiate again: F⃗″(θ) = 2cos(2θ)(î+ĵ). All trigonometric derivatives use radians.'],
 ['Both outputs are scalars: a dot product in (a), a magnitude in (b).', '(a) Multiply corresponding components: f(x) = 2x²−3x²(x+1).', 'Simplify f(x) = −3x³−x².', 'Differentiate to get f′(x) = −9x²−2x.', '(b) Square and add the components: g(x) = √(sin²x+4x²+cos²x).', 'Use sin²x+cos²x = 1, giving g(x) = √(1+4x²), positive everywhere.', 'The chain rule gives g′(x) = 4x/√(1+4x²), for all real x.'],
 ['Use v⃗ = r⃗′, a⃗ = r⃗″, speed |v⃗| and direction v⃗/|v⃗| when velocity is nonzero.', '(a) v⃗(t) = î+2tĵ+2k̂; a⃗(t) = 2ĵ. At 1: v⃗ = î+2ĵ+2k̂, a⃗ = 2ĵ, speed √(1+4+4) = 3, direction (î+2ĵ+2k̂)/3.', '(b) v⃗(t) = −sin tî+cos tĵ+3k̂; a⃗(t) = −cos tî−sin tĵ.', 'At π/4: v⃗ = −î/√2+ĵ/√2+3k̂, a⃗ = −î/√2−ĵ/√2, speed √10, direction (−î/√2+ĵ/√2+3k̂)/√10.', '(c) v⃗(t) = eᵗî−e⁻ᵗĵ+2e²ᵗk̂; a⃗(t) = eᵗî+e⁻ᵗĵ+4e²ᵗk̂.', 'At ln 2, eᵗ = 2, e⁻ᵗ = 1/2, e²ᵗ = 4. Thus v⃗ = 2î−ĵ/2+8k̂ and a⃗ = 2î+ĵ/2+16k̂.', 'The speed is √(4+1/4+64) = √273/2; direction is (4î−ĵ+16k̂)/√273. Each displayed direction has magnitude 1.'],
 ['Put q(t) = |F⃗(t)|, which is positive because F⃗(t) ≠ 0.', 'The squared norm is q² = F⃗·F⃗.', 'Differentiate with the dot-product rule: 2qq′ = F⃗′·F⃗ + F⃗·F⃗′ = 2F⃗·F⃗′.', 'Therefore q′ = (F⃗·F⃗′)/q.', 'Differentiate the normalized vector F⃗/q with the scalar quotient rule: (F⃗/q)′ = F⃗′/q − q′F⃗/q².', 'Substitute the norm derivative: (F⃗/q)′ = F⃗′/q − [(F⃗·F⃗′)F⃗]/q³, as required.', 'The nonzero hypothesis permits every denominator. Differentiating the identity |F⃗/q|² = 1 also shows that this derivative is perpendicular to the unit direction vector.']
]
ANSWERS=['(a) î+2tĵ+(1+3t²)k̂; (b) (1+4s)î+(2s−1)ĵ+2sk̂; (c) −sin θî+cos θĵ−3sin θk̂, cos θ ≠ 0.', '(a) 2î+18tĵ−16k̂; (b) 2î−2ĵ+36s²k̂; (c) −x⁻²î−2k̂, x > 0; (d) 2cos(2θ)(î+ĵ).', '(a) −9x²−2x; (b) 4x/√(1+4x²).', '(a) v⃗ = (1,2,2), a⃗ = (0,2,0), speed 3, direction (1,2,2)/3; (b) v⃗ = (−1/√2,1/√2,3), a⃗ = (−1/√2,−1/√2,0), speed √10, direction v⃗/√10; (c) v⃗ = (2,−1/2,8), a⃗ = (2,1/2,16), speed √273/2, direction (4,−1,16)/√273.', 'The normalized vector derivative equals F⃗′/|F⃗| − [(F⃗·F⃗′)F⃗]/|F⃗|³.']
PAGES=[page('074_page_1.jpg',139,[heading('Example 13 — solution'),paragraph('If the particle’s position at a time t is, then r⃗(t) = costî + sintĵ + t³k̂, then the particle’s velocity and acceleration are:'),eq(r'V⃗(t)=\frac d{dt}[\cos tî+\sin tĵ+t^3k̂]=-\sin tî+\cos tĵ+3t^2k̂'),eq(r'a⃗(t)=\frac{dV⃗}{dt}=\frac d{dt}[-\sin tî+\cos tĵ+3t^2k̂]=-\cos tî-\sin tĵ+6tk̂'),paragraph('The velocity at a time t = 2 is'),eq(r'V⃗(2)=-\sin2î+\cos2ĵ+12k̂\approx-0.91î-0.42ĵ+12k̂'),paragraph('use radians. The acceleration at a time t = 2 is'),eq(r'a⃗(2)=-\cos2î-\sin2ĵ+12k̂\approx0.42î-0.91ĵ+12k̂'),paragraph('The speed is'),eq(r'|V⃗|=\sqrt{(-\sin t)^2+(\cos t)^2+(3t^2)^2}=\sqrt{1+9t^4}'),paragraph('At a time t = 2, the speed is'),eq(r'|V⃗|=\sqrt{1+9(2)^4}=\sqrt{145}'),paragraph('The direction of motion is:'),eq(r'\frac{V⃗}{|V⃗|}=\frac1{\sqrt{145}}[-\sin tî+\cos tĵ+3t^2k̂]'),paragraph('At a time t = 2, the direction of motion is:'),eq(r'\frac{V⃗}{|V⃗|}=\frac1{\sqrt{145}}[-\sin2î+\cos2ĵ+12k̂]\approx-0.91î-0.42ĵ+12k̂'),note('The general direction denominator must be √(1+9t⁴), becoming √145 only at t = 2. The final source decimal vector omits division by √145; the correct unit direction is approximately (−0.075513,−0.034559,0.996546). The path lies on x²+y² = 1 with z = t³, and its speed increases as |t| increases.'),heading('Exercise 5.2')]+[paragraph(str(i+1)+'. '+q) for i,q in enumerate(QUESTIONS)])]
