EXAMPLE={'id':'we-5-source-13','num':'13','title':'Example 13','problem':'For r⃗(t) = cos tî+sin tĵ+t³k̂, find velocity, speed, direction and acceleration at t = 2; interpret the motion.','given':'A circular horizontal projection and cubic height.','method':'Differentiate twice, evaluate in radians, then normalize velocity.','steps':['Velocity is v⃗(t) = −sin tî+cos tĵ+3t²k̂.','Acceleration is a⃗(t) = −cos tî−sin tĵ+6tk̂.','At 2, velocity is (−sin 2,cos 2,12) ≈ (−0.909297,−0.416147,12).','At 2, acceleration is (−cos 2,−sin 2,12) ≈ (0.416147,−0.909297,12).','Speed is √(sin²t+cos²t+9t⁴) = √(1+9t⁴); at 2 it is √145 ≈ 12.041595.','The direction is (−sin 2,cos 2,12)/√145 ≈ (−0.075513,−0.034559,0.996546), with unit magnitude.','The horizontal projection travels around the unit circle; height is t³. At 2 the particle is moving mostly upward, with an upward acceleration of 12. The source final direction approximation forgets the normalization factor.'],'answer':'v⃗(2) = (−sin 2,cos 2,12); a⃗(2) = (−cos 2,−sin 2,12); speed √145; unit direction v⃗(2)/√145.','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'pageStart':138,'pageEnd':139,'verification':'question and complete source working checked'}]}
